# promise: #314
# The (i) at the end of ⌘T's field is Arc's search-suggestions notice (CommandBar.SearchSuggestionsPrivacyView,
# Arc 1.172.1 measured live): pressed, it gives way to a banner in the bottom row's place, "We talk to your
# search engine to help us suggest results.", with Search Settings… and Dismiss. Search Settings… closes the bar
# and opens Settings ▸ Profiles (the engine and "Include search engine suggestions", in Advanced until #372). Dismiss ends it for good: no (i) on
# the next ⌘T. Until 0.1.37 the (i) was a picture and a click did nothing (#314).
budget rss=600 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=notice
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://action/newTab
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarNotice=state
wait 1
expect-log command bar notice state: pressed true, badge true, banner false, rows [0-5], bar open, dismissed false
cra://debug?commandBarNotice=badge
wait 1
expect-log command bar notice badge: pressed true, badge false, banner true, rows [0-4], bar open, dismissed false
cra://debug?commandBarNotice=settings
wait 1
expect-log command bar notice settings: pressed true, badge .*, bar closed, dismissed false, settings profiles
cra://action/newTab
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarNotice=badge
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarNotice=dismiss
wait 1
expect-log command bar notice dismiss: pressed true, badge false, banner false, rows [0-5], bar open, dismissed true
cra://dismiss
wait 1
cra://action/newTab
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarNotice=state
wait 1
expect-log command bar notice state: pressed true, badge false, banner false, rows [0-5], bar open, dismissed true
